course: dictionary
lesson: 9613
title: Stroll: walking, slow and relaxed
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Stroll is a walking word, but it is not a fast one. «Toad strolls out fresh and says how easy life is now!» Toad is not rushing. He is walking in a calm, happy way, so stroll means to walk slowly, for pleasure.
explain: Look at the words around it. «On long summer evenings the four friends stroll through the Wild Wood» sounds relaxed and fun, not like a race. If you swap in the word walk, the sentence still works, but stroll tells you the walk is easy and unhurried.
explain: Stroll can also be a noun. «Go for a stroll» means take a short, easy walk. In sport talk, «the match was a stroll» means the win was easy, so the context tells you which meaning you need.
fact: Stroll means to walk slowly and in a relaxed way, for pleasure, not in a hurry.
fact: As a noun, a stroll is a slow, relaxed walk, as in «go for a stroll» after a meal.
fact: Informally, «a stroll» means something very easy to win or do, as in «the match was a stroll».
fact: Strolling speed is slow, about 3 to 4 km an hour.
fact: Useful phrases are «take a stroll», «stroll along» and «stroll in».
exercise: «A big hairy spider strolls across the living room carpet, making someone scream.» What does strolls mean here? | Runs away fast | Jumps up and down | Flies high in the air | *Walks slowly and calmly, without hurry
exercise: Dad says, «The match was a stroll.» What does he mean? | It was played in the rain | It was a long, tiring run | *It was very easy to win | It was lost by a big score
exercise: «The Rat suggests a row, a stroll or a picnic.» What is a stroll in this sentence? | A kind of picnic food | *A slow, relaxed walk | A race to the finish | A fast, hurried run
test: «Toad strolls out fresh and says how easy life is now!» Which word means the same as strolls here? | Shouts loudly | Rushes in a panic | Sleeps all day | *Walks slowly and happily
test: What does «go for a stroll» mean? | Sit down and rest for an hour | Climb a steep hill | *Take a short, relaxed walk | Run a race around the park
exam: Which sentence uses stroll to mean something very easy? | «The race was so long we nearly gave up.» | «The river rushed fast over the rocks.» | «He ran the whole way to school.» | *«The match was a stroll, and we won easily.»
